<br />
If mamas tell their babies about the blackout of ought-five, they will not speak of a whole region plunged into darkness, as in 2003, nor of a city united, in contrast to the riots of decades before. Instead, they will tell of a weird, hot, sometimes inspiring, mostly frustrating sunny day on Lafayette Avenue in Fort Greene, Brooklyn.<br />
