<h4 class="byline">A ride with a family</h4>

<p>

Here's John Henry Doucette, sweet and tight, on <a href="http://home.hamptonroads.com/stories/story.cfm?story=92865&ran=28994">a family making copies of a dead kid's picture:</a> <br />
<br />
Billie A. Spruill sifted through photos to pick out the best one of her dead son. She and her husband, Robert, were following the advice of a police officer. They traveled in their motor home to a copy shop.<br />
<br />
Her son, Michael L. DeMasse , was killed late Dec. 10 in a hit-and-run collision while riding his motorcycle.<br />
<br />
The Chesapeake man had been trying to turn left from Portsmouth Boulevard onto California Avenue. He was 31 .<br />
<br />
He died near a Christmas tree lot. One witness saw a dark-colored pickup truck with big tires and a loud exhaust system keep going.<br />
<br />
<br />

