<br />
"At the same time, each week smaller papers across the nation quietly publish compelling, thought-provoking pieces of journalism, stories that inform and illuminate. But it's nearly impossible to catch it all; even for those of us who cover the reporters who cover the news, time is often short. And so, in keeping with the season, we give to you <a href="http://www.cjrdaily.org/behind_the_news/five_great_stories_you_didnt_r.php">our countdown of five excellent newspaper stories of 2005 that you might have missed</a> (as we did, until now) -- our way of focusing some attention on outstanding work done this year that was largely overlooked on the national stage."<br />
