In the front yards of homes all over Greater Memphis, the last vestiges of Friday's 3 to 5 inches of snowfall were thawing to death. <br />
 <br />
Wind and sun and 50-degree temperatures had sculpted some into inaccessible pieces of modern art. Others looked like white zombies, frozen in mid-stagger. <br />
