<a href="http://www.nytimes.com/2006/10/04/nyregion/05applecnd.html?_r=1&oref=slogin">Obit here</a>: R. W. Apple Jr., who in more than 40 years as a correspondent and editor at The New York Times wrote about war and revolution, politics and government, food and drink, and the revenge of living well from more than 100 countries, died early this morning in Washington. He was 71.<br />
