<a href="http://gangrey.com/580">
<h2 class="design">11 Days To Nieman</h2></a>
<h4 class="byline">Variety of expression</h4>

<p>

E.L. Callihan in <a href="http://www.amazon.com/Grammar-Journalists-E-L-Callihan/dp/0801968232">Grammar for Journalists</a>: Variety is the spice not only of life but also of good writing. You can keep a reader reading by varying sentence structure and by using other devices to obtain variety in the expression of your ideas.<br />
<br />
The subject of variety of sentence structure has been treated throughout this book. Remember that you can avoid monotonous writing in the following ways:<br />
<br />
By varying the beginings of sentences and ends of paragraphs.<br />
<br />
By using varied kinds of sentences of varied lengths.<br />
<br />
By using direct quotations.<br />
<br />
By using fresh figures of speech.<br />
<br />
By using simple, concrete words. 
