<a href="http://gangrey.com/631">
<h2 class="design">Clear Targets Are Few</h2></a>
<h4 class="byline">More Chivers In Iraq</h4>

<p>

<a href="http://www.nytimes.com/2006/11/22/world/middleeast/22sniper.html?hp&ex=1164258000&en=67ddd7e38efdb2ce&ei=5094&partner=homepage">From Wednesday's NYT</a>: The sniper team left friendly lines hours ahead of the sun. They were a group of marines walking through the chill, hoping to be in hiding before the mullahs&#8217; predawn call to prayer would urge this city awake.<br />
<br />
They reached an abandoned building. Two marines stepped inside, swept the ground floor and signaled to the others to follow them to the flat roof, where they crawled to spots along its walls in which they had previously chiseled out small viewing holes.<br />
<br />
Out came their gear: a map, spotting scopes, binoculars, two-way radios and stools. The snipers took their places, peering through the holes, watching an Iraqi neighborhood from which insurgents often fire. They were hoping an insurgent would try to fire on this day. The waiting began.
