<h4 class="byline">33-part serial in the Rocky Mountain News</h4>

<p>

At 7:59 a.m. on Dec. 14, 1961, a passenger train smashed into a school bus in the farm country of Weld County, instantly killing 20 children. <br />
     <br />
It was the deadliest traffic accident in Colorado history, leaving behind 17 survivors and a devastated community. <br />
     <br />
