<h4 class="byline">personal narratives</h4>

<p>

Fascinating stuff, including this <a href="http://www.nytimes.com/2007/05/22/health/psychology/22narr.html?em&ex=1180152000&en=4499107900694ba8&ei=5087%0A">golden nugget</a>: <i>&#8220;When we first started studying life stories, people thought it was just idle curiosity &#8212; stories, isn&#8217;t that cool?&#8221; said Dan P. McAdams, a professor of psychology at Northwestern and author of the 2006 book, &#8220;The Redemptive Self.&#8221; &#8220;Well, we find that these narratives guide behavior in every moment, and frame not only how we see the past but how we see ourselves in the future.&#8221;<br />
<br />
