<br />
Mr. Niyazov was more complicated, of course, than this. While his salutations to the cowed population might have been polite, he restricted travel and allowed no opposition, free speech, public assembly, fair elections or independent news media. Perceived enemies disappeared into psychiatric wards or jails, and many have never been heard from again. </i>
