Mr. Cherry had no plans to gamble. He is what is known as a rider, one of dozens of New Yorkers &#8212; often homeless or nearly homeless &#8212; who travel back and forth between Chinatown and Atlantic City or Connecticut each day, and sometimes twice a day. They sleep through the two-and-a-half-hour rides and make a quick buck off the casinos without handling so much as a single chip. </i>
