<a href="http://online.wsj.com/public/article/SB118670164592393622.html?mod=blog">Alexandra Alter</a>: <i>On a scorching July afternoon, as the temperature creeps toward 118 degrees in a quiet suburb east of Phoenix, Ric Hoogestraat sits at his computer with the blinds drawn, smoking a cigarette. While his wife, Sue, watches television in the living room, Mr. Hoogestraat chats online with what appears on the screen to be a tall, slim redhead.<br />
<br />
