<p>

There's something beautiful about this one. <a href="http://www.sptimes.com/2007/09/15/Hillsborough/Fired_up_over_his_rig.shtml">Colleen Jenkins</a>: <i>TAMPA - Tod Redman Stewart says he doesn't have a future or much of a life. He lost his freedom, too, Friday to protect his right to burn an American flag. <br />
<br />
Stewart, 32, is not the man you might expect to fight for constitutional rights. He is unemployed, goes in and out of jail. A judge deemed him incompetent after a previous flag burning display. <br />
<br />
He chose the sidewalk in front of the federal courthouse as his protest ground but was not the main attraction. Television crews ignored him, having gathered to report on a bond hearing for a man accused of transporting explosives. <br />
<br />
With the help of an attorney, the man inside would challenge the government's right to detain him. <br />
<br />
The man on the sidewalk did the same, with only a flag and a flame as his armor. <br />
<br />
"You can detain me against my will while you figure this out?" Stewart asked. </i>
