Cowboy Torres and Vivian Brown had been the middle-aged First Couple of the city&#8217;s homeless. By the time Arturo started living at the Forbiten City &#8211; the misspelled name emblazoned on one wall here by some long-forgotten squatter &#8211; on Newburgh&#8217;s riverfront, Cowboy and Vivian were drifting apart. He was moving on.
