<br />
A sofa, its soaked innards about to burst its blue upholstery. A big-screen TV. A sack of lentils. A poster for the classic movie "Easy Rider," a red picture frame, a green bicycle. And a soggy, stained Webster's dictionary, one of humanity's major efforts to capture its own culture. Ruined.<br />
<br />
Off to the side of the pile stood a refrigerator once owned by two people in love. It still carried a magnet that said, "Happily ever after. Always and forever."<br />
<br />
Love may be eternal, but refrigerators obviously aren't.
