Those who remain should picture a miniature kitchen chair, barely an inch high, painted blinding yellow. Now picture it walking.<br />
<br />
The yellow chair walks on its two front legs around a flat stone at the center of a gallery in the Dunedin Fine Art Center. The room holds several other pieces, but when you step inside, it is the chair that catches your gaze.<br />
<br />
The chair is alive.
