<a href="http://gangrey.com/1417">
<h2 class="design">Remembering Mike</h2></a>
<h4 class="byline">and facing forward</h4>

<p>
<a href="http://gangrey.com/1417/img_Jan_11_2008_23_36?display=medium"><img src="http://gangrey.com/1417/img_Jan_11_2008_23_36?display=xsmall" alt="img_Jan_11_2008_23_36" height="110" width="200" border="0" style="border: 1px solid black; float: left; margin-right: 1em; margin-bottom: .5em; padding: 0px;" /></a>
Mike Levine taught a bunch of us how to write. Then he died, on Jan. 14, 2007.<br />
<br />
A group of folks in Middletown, N.Y., where Mike Edited the <a href="http://www.recordonline.com">Times Herald-Record</a>, are honoring him with a <a href="http://www.mikelevineworkshop.org/">column read-a-thon</a> tomorrow and Sunday to raise money for the <a href="http://www.mikelevineworkshop.org/index.php?section=4">Mike Levine Workshop</a>, which has yet to be scheduled but will likely be one of the best intimate workshops in the country. <br />
<br />
They've asked those of us in far-strung places to join the read-a-thon via YouTube. I wanted to share those, if you care to stare at our ugly mugs. Here's <a href="http://www.youtube.com/watch?v=YCkfAVtQfv4">Michael's</a>. And here's <a href="http://www.youtube.com/watch?v=YFn6dhaobE8">mine</a>.<br />
<br />
If you don't, check out some of Mike's columns for inspiration. You'll find a rare breed of watchdog journalism, community advocacy, human compassion and writing style. The columns are <a href="http://www.recordonline.com/apps/pbcs.dll/section?Category=NEWS27">here</a> (scroll down).<br />
<br />
And please consider making a contribution to the <a href="http://www.mikelevineworkshop.org/index.php?section=4">fund</a>. 
