&#8220;Please put it in a trash can,&#8221; riders are reminded. After which Neil Neches, an erudite writer in the transit agency&#8217;s marketing and service information department, inserted a semicolon. The rest of the sentence reads, &#8220;that&#8217;s good news for everyone.&#8221;<br />
