<br />
How much is his safety worth?<br />
<br />
The state of Indiana measured some of the loss with 30-year prison sentences for two of the three robbers who broke through Skaggs' back door and smashed his face with a baseball bat and a bedside lamp.<br />
<br />
But his hospital bills now climb well into the six-figure range. Skaggs has no health insurance, and only a small portion is covered by the Department of Veterans Affairs, a small thanks for his Army service in Vietnam.<br />
<br />
Skaggs, 63, said he walks &#8220;with what I have.&#8221; That is a skill he said he has always possessed.<br />
<br />
And to those burglars who nearly took his life, he offers something priceless - forgiveness.
