<a href="http://www.tampabay.com/news/humaninterest/article899696.ece">Jodie Tillman</a>: PORT RICHEY &#8212; Not quite 8 years old, Alex Gualemi has saddled up a horse, ridden a motorcycle and flown in a single-engine plane. But he yearned, too, for a more simple experience: He wanted to see snow.<br />
<br />
In real life.<br />
<br />
He had seen it on television, heard about it from his dad, who went up north one time. But his boots had never crunched through it; his hands had never molded it into the perfect wintry weapon.<br />
<br />
Geography represented more than a temporary inconvenience. <br />
<br />
 <br />
<a href="http://www.tampabay.com/features/humaninterest/article898516.ece">Lane DeGregory</a>: GULFPORT &#8212; She wrapped the World's Ugliest Dog in a blue baby blanket and carried him outside. But even in the sun, Gus couldn't stop shivering. <br />
<br />
"Hey, little guy," she said softly. "You want to go for a ride?" <br />
<br />
Gus looked up at her and blinked his one bulbous eye. His three paws were curled, claw-like, into his bony body. <br />
<br />
In June, when he was crowned in California, he became an instant celebrity. He growled at Howard Stern, appeared on the Today show and Fox &amp; Friends. Everyone agreed he couldn't look worse.  
