<h4 class="byline">the claws of backhoes, disturbing the earth</h4>

<p>

<a href="http://www.nytimes.com/2008/12/22/us/22land.html?_r=1&ref=us">Dan Barry</a>: EAST PROVIDENCE, R.I.<br />
<br />
They came for the gravely ill racketeer last month, appearing at his North Providence home around dawn. His time was near, but not as near as the police officers at his door. He went peacefully.<br />
<br />
Soon he was at state police headquarters, where veteran detectives knew him well: Nicholas Pari, once the smart-dressing mobster whose nickname, &#8220;Nicky,&#8221; had clearly not taxed the Mafia muse. Now 71, with gauze wrapped around his cancer-ruined neck: Nicky Pari.<br />
<br />
The arrest, for running a crime ring from a flea market, put him in a reflective mood, and he said some things he clearly needed to say, including that he was dying. Still, ever-faithful to that perverse code of the streets, he seemed insulted when asked about the deeds of others.
