<a href="http://gangrey.com/1955">
<h2 class="design">The Mike Levine Workshop</h2></a>
<h4 class="byline">April 30 to May 3</h4>

<p>

Colleagues and family members of the late newspaperman Mike Levine have announced that applications are now being taken for the first Mike Levine Writers Workshop. Journalists must apply by March 1.<br />
<br />
The four-day workshop is scheduled for April 30 to May 1, 2009 at the Shandelee Lake Inn in Livingston Manor, NY. Journalists with 3 to 8 years of experience are eligible to apply. A class of 20 journalists will be chosen to attend the workshop tuition-free; they will work in teams led by 10 journalists who were colleagues of Levine's and who are now working at news organizations that include the New York Post, Boston Globe, Albany Times-Union and St. Petersburg (Florida) Times.<br />
<br />
From 1980 to 2006, Mike Levine worked as a columnist and editor at the Times Herald-Record in New York's Hudson Valley. He died suddenly of a heart attack at the age of 54. The Mike Levine Journalism Education Fund, which is host of the workshop, was established in Levine's memory.  <br />
<br />
The workshop has been organized in order to perpetuate the principles and passions of Levine who became known as an eloquent champion of the people during his career.<br />
<br />
The workshop is guided by the principles and values of Mike Levine and is aimed at breathing new life and solid skills into the work of promising journalists through four days of hands-on coaching and writing.  <br />
<br />
A generous grant from James H. Ottaway Jr. and contributions from Mike Levine's family, friends, colleagues and readers are making the first year of the workshop possible. The Mike Levine Journalism Education Fund is a component fund of the Community Foundation of Orange and Sullivan which is a non-profit organization. <br />
<br />
Noted author and journalist Pete Hamill, who had a personal friendship with Levine will give a keynote address, open to the public, on Friday, May 1, 2009, as part of the first workshop. Hamill's address will take place at 7 p.m. in Jeffersonville.  For more information on the workshop, <a href="http://www.mikelevineworkshop.org/">go here</a>.
