<a href="http://gangrey.com/2019">
<h2 class="design">Carrying Water</h2></a>
<h4 class="byline">'learn something about writing'</h4>

<p>

Everybody I've talked to about <a href="http://www.washingtonpost.com/wp-dyn/content/article/2009/02/27/AR2009022701549.html?hpid=topnews&sid=ST2009030602446">this Weingarten piece</a> has pretty much the same response: <br />
<br />
<i>impressed, inspired -- but also terrified, that I'll never do something that good.</i><br />
<br />
There are a folderfull of stories that spark that same feeling -- a feeling not much different from staring at the stars on a dark night.<br />
<br />
<a href="http://www.washingtonpost.com/wp-dyn/articles/A99301-1994Apr28.html">Von Drehle on Nixon</a>. <a href="http://www.washingtonpost.com/wp-srv/opinions/articles/sept_11_2001.html">Maraniss after Sept. 11</a>. <a href="http://pqasb.pqarchiver.com/washingtonpost/access/80530386.html?dids=80530386:80530386&FMT=ABS&FMTS=ABS:FT&date=Sep+13%2C+2001&author=Hank+Stuever&pub=The+Washington+Post&edition=&startpage=C.01&desc=On+a+Mundane+Morning%2C+The+Clock+Struck+9">Stuever on 9 o'clock</a>. <a href="http://sports.espn.go.com/espn/print?id=3274529&type=story">Death of a Racehorse</a>.<br />
<br />
Years after that last one, W.C. Heinz told <a href="http://sports.espn.go.com/espn/print?id=3274529&type=story">Gare Joyce</a>: "If young writers appreciate my work now, that's a positive," he told me. "I hope they learn something about writing."<br />
<br />
Maybe that's why these hit me like they do. They make me want desperately to be better.<br />
<br />
What's yours?
