<br />
Shelbi Dominguez was 10 when she started worrying about the Chair. Her older sister Sasha had spent 2006 in it, learning Hebrew for her bat mitzvah. Just try to picture Cantor Friedler &#8212; 12 feet tall, perched behind a desk 20 feet long, blazing black eyes barely peering over his massive golden Torah.<br />
<br />
A year ago, Shelbi's bat mitzvah was scheduled for today. To reach the congregation podium, she had to get past the Cantor. She knew one thing about him:<br />
<br />
"He made kids cry."
