<h4 class="byline">'what we need are stories'</h4>

<p>

<a href="http://niemanstoryboard.us/2009/10/13/the-future-of-print-narratives/">Tom Hallman's thoughts</a> (thanks, Dan): Sam&#8217;s story took two trips to Boston. Each day it ran on Page 1 and had two full pages in the A section, across four days. In addition to the logistical things about cost, you couldn&#8217;t get that kind of space now. But good narrative doesn&#8217;t have to take months to do.<br />
<br />
I&#8217;m all for other media when it works, but the online component would have ruined that story. The power of the story doesn&#8217;t come from talking to the doctors or having a graphic to show where the surgeons went in and how many procedures they did. Nobody cares about that&#8212;they care about the boy having a journey.<br />
<br />
If we want to compete with other people in other media, if we just try to do it faster, it&#8217;s a losing battle. The way we can define ourselves is by telling stories.
