<a href="http://gangrey.com/2629">
<h2 class="design">Story Call</h2></a>
<h4 class="byline">for radiolab</h4>

<p>

Have anything that fits this? Email Pat Walters at pkwalters@gmail.com<br />
<br />
<i>We&#8217;re doing a live show about symmetry and mirrors, as you can probably imagine, we&#8217;ve got plenty of mathy and science-y ideas to play with. We&#8217;ll be talking about the tiny asymmetry between matter and anti-matter at the very beginning of the universe that led to the &#8220;all matter, all the time&#8221; universe we all inhabit. We&#8217;ll explore the gene in almost every creature that dictates right and left. We&#8217;ll learn about the handed-ness of the molecules that make up life, hair parts and crooked smiles, the nature of beauty, and the sinister nature of the world in the mirror. <br />
<br />
But we&#8217;re still in search of a good ole yarn to spin. So we&#8217;re on the hunt for a personal, first-person story that somehow reflects some idea of symmetry or asymmetry. Maybe it&#8217;s about two halves being separated, or coming back together. Maybe it&#8217;s about something that looks perfectly matched, except for some tiny asymmetry that ends up making a big difference. Twins and love seem like obvious routes to go, but then again, we don&#8217;t want to go the obvious route. So if it&#8217;s a twin or a love story, it&#8217;ll need a pretty surprising twist, or just be too darn compelling to ignore.</i>
