<a href="http://gangrey.com/2774">
<h2 class="design">Mailbag!</h2></a>
<h4 class="byline">send your stories</h4>

<p>

Ben,<br />
<br />
I'm hoping to get some help from the Gangrey.com community. <br />
<br />
Mike Sager and I are just beginning to put together an anthology collecting the finest literary journalism being done by "the next generation." That's a pretty flexible category, I know, but we are thinking of work done in the last 5-10 years by people who today are under 40 years old or so. I'm tentatively calling the book, "Young Wave: America's Next Generation of Fine Literary Journalists." We want to put out a wide net, collecting nominations from newspapers, magazines, nonfiction literary journals, websites. Mike and I are struck by the continued passion the new generation has for the work and want to help make the wider journalism community and the next, next generation of journalism students know that such work continues and is possible in the new media era.<br />
<br />
The rule for entry is that the pieces adhere to the highest standards of literal accuracy.<br />
<br />
As a practical matter, it would be a big help if nominations came with: 1) Writer's name; 2) phone numbers; 3) emails; 4) article title; and 5) place and date of publication.<br />
<br />
Please forward suggestions to me at wharring@illinois.edu.<br />
<br />
Thanks.<br />
<br />
Walt Harrington
