<h4 class="byline">dept. of education</h4>

<p>

I've stood on Mount Petit Jean before, when I had abs and hair. God's country. Me and my coonass buddy, Lance, tried to guess how far it was to the most distant bluegray bump on the horizon.<br />
<br />
"Two hundred miles," he said.<br />
<br />
"Fifteen miles," I said.<br />
<br />
We made some ridiculous bet and went inside the camp station to ask the ranger. I won. Eighty eight miles. <br />
<br />
<a href="http://summit.oxfordamerican.org/">This week-long summit for "ambitious writers"</a> on top of Petit Jean costs a bunch -- we're talking used Hyundai Accent money -- but looks pretty sweet. Nature trails. Southern food. Music. And this: <br />
<br />
<i>Confirmed faculty members include Wells Tower (recently named by the New Yorker as among the 20 best fiction writers under 40); Kevin Brockmeier (one of Granta magazine&#8217;s Best Young American Novelists and winner of the O. Henry Award); Pico Iyer (praised by Time as &#8220;among the finest travel writers of his generation&#8221;); as well as Tom Franklin, Cristina Henr&iacute;quez, Scott Huler, and Jay Jennings.</i><br />
<br />
I'd love to shoot the shit with Tom Franklin. See how far he thinks it is to that mountain over there.
